    {"id": "round-numbers", "corpus": "corpus/round-numbers.json", "ctrace": "round-numbers.ctrace"}
  ],
  "fixtures_order_note": "`special-tokens` is FIRST on purpose. Both harnesses build the fixtures in this order inside ONE process, so every other fixture is tokenized after a block containing a literal `<|endoftext|>`. That makes the 'no silent estimate fallback' assertion (tests/test_golden.py::test_fixtures_really_run_the_exact_tokenizer and its JS twin) a live regression test for the process-wide latch this corpus once had to route around: if a per-text tokenizer refusal ever leaks back into the encoder, every fixture below turns into estimates and the suite fails immediately. Nothing else depends on the order — each fixture is an independent file with its own cases.",

